A||N||6||Call||Question On A Rebuilding A Fiero Engine||||5||
Z||000000||Call||01-17-2000||02:57 PM||||How much does it cost to rebuild a Fiero engine? Thanks ahead of time!||||reg||5
Z||000001||87PegasusGT||01-17-2000||03:12 PM||||I don't know if you are planning on buying everything seperate, but Fiero store has a rebuild kit for $699 with a performance rebuild option at $899.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||01-17-2000||06:51 PM||||I bought a Grooms long block from Ed Parks at the Fiero Factory for $1175.  It is bored .040 and comes with an unlimited mileage 18 month warranty and all of the gaskets to put it back together.<P>So far it feels great.  While I had it apart I ported the exhaust and intake manifolds, rebuilt the distributor,  and repainted everything.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||01-17-2000||07:36 PM||||If those prices seem high, here is some perspective. I just got my car back from a shop here in Oklahoma (cheap COL) that did a rebuild for me. The original quote with a 1 year 14k mi warranty was in the ballpark of $1400.  After all was said and done, I gave them a check for $2700. They did use all forged bits and pieces instead of cash, added a new water pump, clutch,harmonic balancer, and stripped and powdercoated my intake and valve covers. Of course they raped me on parts cost, so if you have the tools and space, (and know how) then all told you may be able to actually get away with aroud $1000.  It shore is purty tho!||||reg||1
Z||000004||la9||01-18-2000||01:58 AM||||I figure to have around $1500 in my 2.8 rebuild. That is with everything new except valves and rocker arms. As you will find out you can get a rebuilt engine cheaper than doing it yourself and get a much better warranty. On the plus side you'll know your engine wasn't built with profit in mind by doing it yourself.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierosound||01-19-2000||05:08 PM||||CALL<P>You might also check into swapping in a low mileage 3.4 from a wrecked car.   This auto wrecker in the south-eastern US has GM V6 long block engines with variuos mileage for $350-450.  You may want to see if they have anything you can use.<P> <A HREF="http://www.tacreationsusa.com/v6.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tacreationsusa.com/v6.htm</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Linx||01-21-2000||10:48 PM||||I just priced a 2.8 for $1629.  Heads included.  Jasper Engines warrents their engine for 75k or 3 years.  Incredible.  800-827-7455||||reg||1
